New option `--trait-rank-decreases`: in `decreases` clauses, values of a trait that is not a reference type are ordered by structural rank together with inductive datatypes and sequences (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/317). A datatype that extends such a trait can then recurse through its trait-typed fields: `decreases this` in the datatype is comparable with `decreases this` in the trait member. With `--additional-axioms`, a trait-typed field of an inductive datatype value is below that value, which most such programs also need. Trait members without a `decreases` clause still need an explicit `decreases this`. The option has no effect with `--legacy-decreases-order` and is disabled by default.
